{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And you will not bear for the place.</b> Like the sense of \"you will forgive,\" as in \"bearing iniquity\" (Exodus 34:7)." "\"For the place\" is Sodom, for on its account Abraham drew near to rescue Lot."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Resolved למקום as 'for the place' (rather than as the divine epithet 'the Place'), since the following comment identifies it as Sodom."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:59.160871314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}